<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('../partials/head') %></head>
<body class="mll-page">
  <%- include('../partials/header') %>
  <main class="mll-home">
    <h1>Admin setup</h1>
    <p class="mll-hero__lead">OAuth isn't configured yet. Two short steps to enable Google login for the admin console.</p>

    <section class="mll-chart-block">
      <h2>1 · Google Cloud Console</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <a href="https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Cloud Console → Credentials</a></li>
        <li>Create credentials → <strong>OAuth 2.0 Client ID</strong> → Application type <strong>Web application</strong></li>
        <li>Add this <strong>Authorized redirect URI</strong>:
          <pre class="mll-code"><%= callbackUrl %></pre>
        </li>
        <li>Copy the <strong>Client ID</strong> and <strong>Client Secret</strong></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mll-chart-block">
      <h2>2 · Create <code>.env</code></h2>
      <p>At <code>/srv/mllPitches/.env</code>:</p>
      <pre class="mll-code">GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...your client id...
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...your client secret...
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=<%= callbackUrl %>
SESSION_SECRET=...a long random string...
ADMIN_EMAIL=<%= adminEmail %></pre>
      <p>Then restart the tmux session:</p>
      <pre class="mll-code">tmux send-keys -t mllpitches C-c
tmux send-keys -t mllpitches "PORT=3608 npm start" Enter</pre>
    </section>

    <section class="mll-chart-block">
      <h2>3 · Sign in</h2>
      <p>Go to <a href="/admin">/admin</a> — you'll be redirected to Google. Only <strong><%= adminEmail %></strong> is accepted.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <%- include('../partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
